  "source": {
    "description": "The owner-approved reusable Figma Tones collection, supplied on 2026-10-23 as sRGB HEX after conversion, already using the background/foreground naming: tone-<name> is the soft background and tone-<name>-foreground the text or icon colour on it. These values are authoritative. The earlier OKLCH reference (secuna-frontend-experiment src/styles/semantic.css, where tone-<name>-soft was the background) was a starting point only and is neither committed nor read.",
    "purpose": "Identity or category, primarily initials-based avatar fallbacks. Not status, severity or branding.",
    "synchronization": "None. Figma and these defaults are kept in step by hand.",
    "naming": "Ordinal, colour-agnostic names: the Figma rows Blue, Orange, Purple, Pink, Teal and Violet are tones 1 to 6 in that order (tone-1 / tone-1-foreground through tone-6 / tone-6-foreground). Stored themes using the earlier colour-word names are renamed on load with their values kept."
  },
  "precisionPolicy": {
    "color": "Canonical OKLCH through packages/core/src/theme/color.ts normalizeColor (HEX -> sRGB -> OKLCH, 6 decimal places). Every sRGB HEX value lies inside the Display P3 gamut, so all 24 values are admitted unchanged; each normalized value is a fixed point of the normalizer and renders back to its source HEX."
  },
  "defaultsPolicy": "Shared: every theme without a stored tones field renders these values (TONE_DEFAULTS in packages/core/src/theme/schema.ts). The first tone edit stores the complete resolved set on that theme.",
